# Exercise order

A guide is a sequence. Later exercises depend on earlier ones. Validate and execute steps in printed order.

1. Setup, then Exercise 1, then Exercise 2, then Exercise 3, and so on.
2. Inside an exercise, finish tasks and steps in the order they appear. Do not open a later exercise while an earlier one still has an unfinished step.
3. A step is finished only when it is PASS, a real mismatch or failure, or explicitly blocked. Do not skip it to keep moving.
4. If a later exercise was already touched, go back and finish the earliest unfinished step before treating later work as next.
5. Write the pass/fail summary only after every step in the guide has a final status.

Example: if Exercise 2-2 still has an unfinished action, do not continue Exercise 3 until 2-2 is finished.
